Earthquake Analysis and Prediction
Project Overview

Developed a Machine Learning-based project to analyze historical earthquake data from 1990 to 2023, identify earthquake-related patterns, and classify earthquake risk levels using data analysis and predictive modelling techniques.

Objectives
- Analyze historical earthquake datasets.
- Perform data cleaning and preprocessing.
- Apply feature engineering.
- Build Machine Learning models.
- Evaluate model performance.
Technologies Used
- Python
- Pandas and NumPy
- Matplotlib and Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- Machine Learning
Project Workflow
1. Data Collection – Collected historical earthquake data.
2. Data Preprocessing – Handled missing values and prepared the dataset.
3. EDA – Analyzed earthquake patterns and distributions.
4. Feature Engineering – Prepared relevant features for modelling.
5. Model Building – Developed Machine Learning models.
6. Evaluation – Used confusion matrix, accuracy, precision and recall.
Project Outcome

Analyzed historical earthquake patterns and evaluated Machine Learning models for earthquake risk classification.
